Standard Python/Flask .gitignore

---------------------------------

1. Python Compiled/Dependency Files

---------------------------------

pycache/          # Directory for compiled Python modules (seen everywhere)
*.pyc                 # Compiled Python files (e.g., attendance.cpython-312.pyc)
__pycache__/
*.o
*.so
*.egg
*.dist-info/
blog_content/
static_blog/
build/
dist/

---------------------------------

2. Virtual Environments (MANDATORY)

---------------------------------

Prevents committing large dependency folders.

venv/
env/
.venv/
conda_env/

---------------------------------

3. Database & Secret Configuration

---------------------------------

IMPORTANT: Prevents committing API keys, database credentials, and local database files.

.env                  # Common for environment variables
.flaskenv
instance/             # Flask instance folder (often holds configuration or SQLite DBs)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

---------------------------------

4. Logs and Temporary Files

---------------------------------

*.log                 # Log files
*.save                # Files ending in .save (like attendance.py.save, base.html.save)
celerybeat-schedule   # Celery scheduling state file
cmds.txt             # Temporary command file
*.qmd                 # Quarto/R Markdown files (like email.qmd)
*.save                # Files ending in .save (like attendance.py.save)
*.sh                  # Shell scripts (like git.initial.sh)
schedule/             # Celery

---------------------------------

5. IDEs and OS Files

---------------------------------

.idea/                # PyCharm/IntelliJ configuration
.vscode/              # VS Code settings
.DS_Store             # macOS system files
*~                    # Emacs/Vim temporary backup files

---------------------------------

6. Uploads and Generated Assets

---------------------------------

Files uploaded by users that should NOT be tracked by source control.

If 'uploads/' contains files, we should ignore all content but keep the folder

so Flask doesn't crash if it expects it to exist.

uploads/*
!uploads/.gitkeep      # If you create a .gitkeep file inside uploads, it will track the empty folder.



*.save
